&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with teams across the organization to understand pain points in their infrastructure usage to find common ideas and work to create solutions which span multiple domains.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and produce high quality written proposals, communications and documentation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute on technical programs that require deep systems and engineering level knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering Managers, Product Managers and other Technical Program Managers to define, scope and drive large programs to conclusion.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a key part in shaping the technical design, predicting technical roadblocks by collaborating with engineers, and identifying trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement, and iterate on program management techniques, frameworks, and KPIs to achieve goals with well-defined success criteria.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Elevate the execution muscle of engineering teams around you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train them to be better at delivery where needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help influence peers / stakeholders and build consensus while dealing with ambiguity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage data and acquired knowledge to drive strategic decisions at an engineering leadership level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create widely circulated plans, driving consistency, clarity and building alignment across teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalize and execute critical cross functional programs spanning multiple engineering organizations for Core Infrastructure (Compute, Networking, Database, Services).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must have a Bachelor&#39;s degree or foreign equivalent in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related field, plus 8 years of experience in Technical Program Management or a related field, of which, at least 5 years must be post bachelor&#39;s progressive experience. Must also have experience in each of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;8 years experience in:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distributed Systems;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Service Oriented Architecture (SOA);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program management during all phases of software development from kick-off to launch;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving internal and external process improvements across multiple teams and functions; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading large-scale efforts across multiple teams and functions;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;6 years experience in core infrastructure including database, cloud compute, networking, and services;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;4 years experience in SQL;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3 years experience in&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Analysis;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud Infrastructure; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developer Productivity or Developer Experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $174,637.00 - $260,200.00/Yr.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary range represents the base salary range for the role and any sales commissions/sales bonuses targets, if applicable, would be in addition to the base salary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 hrs/week&lt;/p&gt;
